  "result": "Perfect! All 131 tests pass. I've successfully added payment terms support to invoice creation.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/errors.js** - Added new error code:\n   - `TERMS_INVALID` - Terms must be one of: NET14, NET30, EOM\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** - Added payment terms:\n   - `calculateDueDate()` helper function:\n     - NET14: issue date + 14 days\n     - NET30: issue date + 30 days\n     - EOM: last day of the issue date's month (handles December correctly)\n   - Updated `createInvoice()` to:\n     - Accept optional `terms` parameter\n     - Default to 'NET30' if not provided\n     - Validate terms is one of the three valid options\n     - Calculate and store `dueDate` on invoice\n\n3. **test/invoices.test.js** - Added 8 comprehensive tests:\n   - Default NET30 terms\n   - NET14 calculation (2026-10-07 \u2192 2026-10-21)\n   - NET30 calculation (2026-10-07 \u2192 2026-11-06)\n   - EOM calculation (2026-10-07 \u2192 2026-10-31)\n   - Invalid terms error handling\n   - EOM on end of month edge case\n   - EOM in December with year transition\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- Terms default to NET30 for backward compatibility\n- EOM correctly handles month/year boundaries (December \u2192 January of next year)\n- Due date calculations use UTC-based date utilities\n- Validation rejects unknown terms before processing",
